## Migration order (recommended)

1. ✅ **log-clean.js** — DONE 2026-05-25. `lib/log_clean.py` + `POST /api/v1/logs/clean`.
2. **branch.js** — biggest single 🔴 leak. Land
   `lib/conversations/branches.py` + `/api/v1/conversations/{id}/branches/*`,
   then replace the JS with thin fetch wrappers.
3. **ui.js tool-round / turn-summary derivation** — emit structured
   server events; UI just renders.
4. **main.js config builders** — consolidate into `lib/api_schema/config.py`.
5. **paper-reader.js / translation.js / image-gen.js polling** — collapse
   into the unified `/api/push` channel + `/api/v1/tasks/{id}/stream`.
6. **myday.js / settings.js / compaction-viewer.js** — derive on the
   server, render on the client.

Each migration is its own commit and lands in this order in subsequent
PRs. The headless API ships now (this commit) and Phase 0 cleanup
follows. The current commit only **documents** the boundary in
`CLAUDE.md §16` so new code can't regress.

---

## Self-test

When adding a new top-level JS file, ask:

> Is the function I'm writing **deciding business policy** (does it run
> a tool, decide retry strategy, build a request body that the model
> sees, decide a derivation rule, persist the canonical version of
> something)? **If yes**, write a server endpoint instead and have JS
> call it.

If the answer is "I'm just calling `fetch()` and rendering the
result", you're on the right side of the boundary.
